(a,b\\) have different parity, they are unequal, so\n\\[\nv_3(3^a+2\\cdot3^b)=r.\n\\]\nBy the lifting-the-exponent formula,\n\\[\nr=v_3(2^{n+1}-1)\n=v_3\\!\\left(4^{(n+1)/2}-1\\right)\n=1+v_3(n+1).\n\\]\nIn particular, \\(3^r\\le3(n+1)\\). Equation (2) therefore implies\n\\[\n3^{n-r}<2^{n+1}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\left(\\frac32\\right)^n<2\\cdot3^r\\le6(n+1).\n\\]\nThis fails at \\(n=11\\), because \\(3^{11}>72\\cdot2^{11}\\), and the ratio\n\\[\n\\frac{(3/2)^n}{n+1}\n\\]\nis increasing for \\(n\\ge2\\). Thus \\(n\\le10\\), leaving only \\(n=3,5,7,9\\).\n\nThe parity conditions and \\(r=1+v_3(n+1)\\) determine \\(a,b\\):\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c}\nn&a&b&3^a+2\\cdot3^b&2^{n+1}-1\\\\ \\hline\n3&2&1&15&15\\\\\n5&2&3&63&63\\\\\n7&6&1&735&255\\\\\n9&8&1&6567&1023\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nFor each successful row, either factor can be \\(m\\), yielding \\(m=9,6\\) for \\(n=3\\), and \\(m=9,54\\) for \\(n=5\\). These all satisfy the original equation.\n\nFinal answer: \\(\\boxed{(m,n)\\in\\{(6,3),(9,3),(9,5),(54,5)\\}}\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":135,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2775,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2070},"total_tokens":2910},"user":null,"metadata":{}}
